{
  "title": "17: al-Israa الإسراء",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nسُبْحٰنَ الَّذِىْۤ اَسْرٰى بِعَبْدِهٖ لَيْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ اِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْاَقْصَا الَّذِىْ بٰرَكْنَا حَوْلَهٗ لِنُرِيَهٗ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(1)\nLAAHE LAZEE AASRAA BEA’ABDEH LAYLAN MENAL MASJEDIL HARAAME ELAL MASJEDIL AL-AAQSAA LAZEE BAARAKNAA HAWLAHU LENUREEH MIN AAYAATENAA INNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L AL-BASEERU.\nGlory be to Him Who carried His servant (Apostle Muhammad) by night from the Holy Mosque (of the Ka’ba) to the Farthest Mosque, which We have blessed its environment that We may show unto him, of Our signs; Verily He, is the All-Hearing, the All-Seeing.\nوَاٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ وَ جَعَلْنٰهُ هُدًى لِّبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اَلَّا تَتَّخِذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِىْ وَكِيْلًا ؕ‏(2)\nWA AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA WA LAW HODAM LLEBANEAA ISRAAA-EELAZ ALLAA TATTAKHEZOOA MIN DOONEAA WAKEELAA.\nAnd gave We unto Moses the Book (Torah) and made it a guidance for the children of Israel, (saying) that “Take ye not other than Me (any one as) a guardian.\nذُرِّيَّةَ مَنْ حَمَلْنَا مَعَ نُوْحٍؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ عَبْدًا شَكُوْرًا‏(3)\nZURREETA MAN HAMALNAA LAAHA NOOHIN INNAHU KAANA A’BDAN SHAKOORAN.\n(O’ ye!) The offspring of those whom We bore with Noah (in the Ark); Verily, he (Noah) was a grateful servant.\nوَقَضَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ فِى الْكِتٰبِ لَتُفْسِدُنَّ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَرَّتَيْنِ وَلَتَعْلُنَّ عُلُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(4)\nWA QAZAYNAA ELAA BANEE AESRAAEELA FIL KETAABE LATUFSEDUNNA FIL ARZE MARRATAYNE WALATAA’LUNNA O’LUWWAN KABEERAA.\nAnd We had (expressly) declared unto the children of Israel (a warning) in the Book (Torah saying): “Certainly ye will make mischief in the land twice, and certainly will ye be elated with great arrogance.\nفَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ اُوْلٰٮهُمَا بَعَثْنَا عَلَيْكُمْ عِبَادًا لَّنَاۤ اُولِىْ بَاْسٍ شَدِيْدٍ فَجَاسُوْا خِلٰلَ الدِّيَارِ ؕ وَكَانَ وَعْدًا مَّفْعُوْلًا‏(5)\nFA-EZAA JAAA-A WAA’DU AOOLAAHUMAA BAA’ASNAA A’LAYKUM E’EBAADAN LANAA OOLEE OOLOO BAA-SIN FAJAASOOA KHELAALA AD-DEEARE KAANAL WA’DAN MMAFU’OOLAN.\nSo when came the first of the two (promises), raised We upon you Our servants, with terrible prowess, so they invaded the innermost parts of your abodes; and it was a warning (completely) fulfilled.\nثُمَّ رَدَدْنَا لَكُمُ الْكَرَّةَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَاَمْدَدْنٰكُمْ بِاَمْوَالٍ وَّبَنِيْنَ وَجَعَلْنٰكُمْ اَكْثَرَ نَفِيْرًا‏(6)\nSUMMA RADADNAA LAKOMUL AL-KARRATA A’LAYHIM WAAMDADNAAKUM BEAAMWAALIN WWABANEENA WA JA-A’LNAAKUM AKSARAN NAFEERAN.\nThen returned We unto you the turn (to prevail) against them and aided you with wealth and offspring and made you a numerous host.\nاِنْ اَحْسَنْتُمْ اَحْسَنْتُمْ لِاَنْفُسِكُمْوَاِنْ اَسَاْتُمْ فَلَهَا ؕ فَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ الْاٰخِرَةِ لِيَسُوْۤءا وُجُوْهَكُمْ وَلِيَدْخُلُوا الْمَسْجِدَ كَمَا دَخَلُوْهُ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّلِيُتَبِّرُوْا مَا عَلَوْا تَتْبِيْرًا‏(7)\nIN AAHSANTUM AAHSANTUM LEAANFUSEKUMWAAN AASAATUM FA LAHAA FA-EZAA JAAA-A WAA’DU AAKHERATE LEESOOA WOJOOHAKUM WALEEDKHULOOA MASJEDIL KAMAA DAKHALOOHU AWWALA MARRAH WWALEETABBEROOA MAA A’ALAWA TATBEERAN.\nIf ye do good, ye do it for your own selves; and if ye do evil it is (in like manner) for your ownselves; So when came the second promise (warning to be fulfilled) (We roused your enemies to) sadden your faces, and that they may enter the Mosque as they entered it the first time, and to destroy whatever they conquered (with) total destruction.\nعَسٰى رَبُّكُمْ اَنْ يَّرْحَمَكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ عُدْتُّمْ عُدْنَاۘ وَجَعَلْنَا جَهَنَّمَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ حَصِيْرًا‏(8)\nA’SAA RABBOKUM AN YYARHAMAKUM WA U’UDTTUM U’UDNAA WA JA-A’LNAA JAHANNAMA LIL KAAFEREENA HASEERAN.\nIt may be that your Lord will have mercy on you, but if ye (again) return (to disobedience) We (too) will return (to chastisement), and We have made Hell for the infidels a prison.\nاِنَّ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ يَهْدِىْ لِلَّتِىْ هِىَ اَقْوَمُ وَ يُبَشِّرُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ اَنَّ لَهُمْ اَجْرًا كَبِيْرًا ۙ‏(9)\nINNAL HAAZAA QURAANA YAHDEE LELLATEAA HEYA AAQWAMU WA YUBASSHERU MOAMENEEN LAZEENA YA’MALOON SAALEHAATE ANNAL LAHUM AJRAN KABEERAA.\nVerily, this Qur’an guideth unto that which is the most upright and announceth glad tidings unto the believers who do good that they shall have a great reward,\nوَّاَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ اَعْتَدْنَا لَهُمْ عَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا‏(10)\nWA ANNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE A-A’TADNAA LAHUM A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAnd those who believe not in the hereafter, We have prepared for them a painful torment.\nوَيَدْعُ الْاِنْسَانُ بِالشَّرِّ دُعَآءَهٗ بِالْخَيْرِ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ عَجُوْلًا‏(11)\nWAYADU’U INSAANO BEALSSHARRE DUA’AAAH BE-KHAYR KAANAL INSAANO A’AJOOLAN.\nAnd prayeth man for evil as he prayeth for good; and man in ever hasty.\nوَجَعَلْنَا الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ اٰيَتَيْنِ فَمَحَوْنَاۤ اٰيَةَ الَّيْلِ وَجَعَلْنَاۤ اٰيَةَ النَّهَارِ مُبْصِرَةً لِّتَبْتَغُوْا فَضْلًا مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَلِتَعْلَمُوْا عَدَدَ السِّنِيْنَ وَالْحِسَابَؕ وَكُلَّ شَىْءٍ فَصَّلْنٰهُ تَفْصِيْلًا‏(12)\nWA JA-A’LNAA LAYLA WAN NAHAARA AAAYATAYNE FAMAHAWNAA AAYATA LAYLE WA JA-A’LNAA AAYATA AN-NAHAARE MUBSERATAN LLETABTAGHOOA FAZLAM MIN RABBEKUM WALETAA’LAMOOA A’ADADA AS-SENEENA WAL HESAABA WA KULLA SHAY-IN FASSALNAAHU TAFSEELAN.\nAnd We have made the night and the day two (of Our) signs, then cause We the sign of the night to pass away and have made We the sign of the day sight-giving that ye may seek grace from your Lord, and that ye may know the number and the count of the years; and every thing have We explained in detail.\nوَكُلَّ اِنْسَانٍ اَلْزَمْنٰهُ طٰۤئِرَهٗ فِىْ عُنُقِهٖؕ وَنُخْرِجُ لَهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ كِتٰبًا يَّلْقٰٮهُ مَنْشُوْرًا‏(13)\nWA KULLA AENSAANIN AALZAMNAAHU TAAERAH FEE U’UNUQEH WANUKHREJU LAHU YAWMA QEYAAMATE KETAABAA YYALQAAHU MANSHOORAN.\nAnd every man’s destiny We have caused to cling to his neck; and We will bring forth unto him on the Day of Resurrection a book which he will find wide open.\nاِقْرَاْ كِتٰبَك َؕ كَفٰى بِنَفْسِكَ الْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكَ حَسِيْبًا ؕ‏(14)\nIQRAA KETAABAK KAFAA BE-TUKHFEE YAWMA A’LAYKA HASEEBAA.\n(It will be said unto him) “Read thou thy book; Sufficeth thine own self today, as a reckoner against thee.\nمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَاِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِىْ لِنَفْسِهٖ ۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَاِنَّمَا يَضِلُّ عَلَيْهَا ؕ وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰى ؕ وَمَا كُنَّا مُعَذِّبِيْنَ حَتّٰى نَبْعَثَ رَسُوْلًا‏(15)\nMANIS TADAA FA-INNAMAA YAHTADEE LENAFSEHI WA MAN ZALLA FA-INNAMAA YAZELLU A’LAYHAA WA LAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA LAHU WA MAA KUNNAA MUA’AZZEBEENA HATTAA NABA’ASA RASOOLAM.\nWhosoever getteth guided aright, verily he getteth guided aright for his ownself; and he who goeth astray, verily he goeth astray against his ownself; nor shall the bearer of a burden bear the burden of another; And We chastise not (any people) until We raise an apostle (among them)\nوَاِذَاۤ اَرَدْنَاۤ اَنْ نُّهْلِكَ قَرْيَةً اَمَرْنَا مُتْرَفِيْهَا فَفَسَقُوْا فِيْهَا فَحَقَّ عَلَيْهَا الْقَوْلُ فَدَمَّرْنٰهَا تَدْمِيْرًا‏(16)\nWA EZAA AARADNAA AN NNUHLEKA QARYATAN AAMARNAA MUTRAFEEHAA FAFASAQOOA FEEHAA FA HAQQA A’LAYHAA QAWLO FADAMMARNAAHAA TADMEERAN.\nAnd when intend We to destroy a town, (first) send We Our commandment to its people who lead easy lives (to obey Us), and yet (when) they transgress in it, then proveth true against it, the word so We destroy it to a complete destruction.\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ نُوْحٍؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ بِذُنُوْبِ عِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(17)\nWA AHLAKNAL MENAL QOROONE MIN BA’DE NOOHIN KAFAA BERABBEKA BEZUNOOBE E’BAADEHI KHABEERAA BASEERAA.\nAnd how many have We destroyed of the peoples after Noah! and thy Lord is (Himself) sufficient with regard to the sins of his servants, (for He is) the All-Aware, the All-Seeing.\nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ الْعَاجِلَةَ عَجَّلْنَا لَهٗ فِيْهَا مَا نَشَآءُ لِمَنْ نُّرِيْدُ ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَا لَهٗ جَهَنَّمَۚ يَصْلٰٮهَا مَذْمُوْمًا مَّدْحُوْرًا‏(18)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO A’AJELATA A’AJJALNAA LAHU FEEHAA MAA NASHAAA-O LEMAN-Y NNUREEDU SUMMA JA-A’LNAA LAHU JAHANNAMA YASLAAHAA MAZMOOMAN MMADHOORAN.\nWhosoever intendeth this (fast hastening) immediate (life) We hasten unto him in it what We please for whomsoever We intend, then assign We unto him the hell; he shall enter it despised, driven away.\nوَمَنْ اَرَادَ الْاٰخِرَةَ وَسَعٰى لَهَا سَعْيَهَا وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ كَانَ سَعْيُهُمْ مَّشْكُوْرًا‏(19)\nWA MAN ARAADA AAKHERATA MOH LAHAA SAA’YAHAA WA HOWA MUMENUN FAAWLAAEKA KAANA SAA’YUHUM MASHKOORAA.\nAnd whosoever intendeth the hereafter and striveth for it a (sincere) striving and he is a believer, these, their striving shall be (recompensed fully) appreciated.\nكُلًّا نُّمِدُّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ وَهٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ مِنْ عَطَآءِ رَبِّكَ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ عَطَآءُ رَبِّكَ مَحْظُوْرًا‏(20)\nKULLAN NNUMEDDU HAAOOLAAA-E WA HAAOOLAAA-E MIN A’ATAAE RABBEKA WA MAA KAANA A’ATAAU RABBEKA MAHZOORAN.\nAll We do aid, these and (also) those out of the bounty of thy Lord; and the bounty of thy Lord is not confined.\nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ ؕ وَلَلْاٰخِرَةُ اَكْبَرُ دَرَجٰتٍ وَّاَكْبَرُ تَفْضِيْلًا‏(21)\nAUNZUR KAYFA FAZZALNAA BA’ZAHUM A’LAA ELAA WA LAL-AAKHERATO AKBARO DARAJAATIN WWAAKBARU TAFZEELAN.\nBehold (thou) how We caused some of them excel the others; and surely the hereafter is much greater in respect of degrees and greater still in respect of excellence.\nلَا تَجْعَلْ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتَقْعُدَ مَذْمُوْمًا مَّخْذُوْلًا‏(22)\nLAA TAJ-A’L LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FATAQU’UDA MAZMOOMAN MMAKHZOOLAN.\nAssociate not with God any other gods, lest thou sittest despised, neglected.\nوَقَضٰى رَبُّكَ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُ وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا ؕ اِمَّا يَبْلُغَنَّ عِنْدَكَ الْكِبَرَ اَحَدُهُمَاۤ اَوْ كِلٰهُمَا فَلَا تَقُلْ لَّهُمَاۤ اُفٍّ وَّلَا تَنْهَرْهُمَا وَقُلْ لَّهُمَا قَوْلًا كَرِيْمًا‏(23)\nWA QAZAA RABBOKA ALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAA IYYAAHO WA BIL-WAALEDAYNE EHSAANANW IMMAA YABLUGHANNA E’ENDAKA AL-KEBARA AAHADUHUMAA AW KELAAHUMAA FALAA TAQUL LAHOMAA AUFFIN WA LAA TANHARHUMAA WA QUL LAHOMAA QAWLAM KAREEMAA.\nAnd commanded thy Lord hath that thou shalt worship not (any one) but Him, and goodness to parents; if either or both of them reach old age with thee, utter not unto them (even so much as) “Fie” nor chide them, and speak unto them a generous word.\nوَاخْفِضْ لَهُمَا جَنَاحَ الذُّلِّ مِنَ الرَّحْمَةِ وَقُلْ رَّبِّ ارْحَمْهُمَا كَمَا رَبَّيٰنِىْ صَغِيْرًا ؕ‏(24)\nWAAKHFEZ LAHOMAA JANAAHA AZ-ZULLE MENAL AR-RAHMATE WA QUL RABBIL ARHAMHUMAA KAMAA RABBAYNEAA AW.\nAnd lower unto them the wing of humility out of compassion, and say thou: “O’ My Lord! Have mercy on them as they cherished me when I was little.\nرَّبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا فِىْ نُفُوْسِكُمْؕ اِنْ تَكُوْنُوْا صٰلِحِيْنَ فَاِنَّهٗ كَانَ لِلْاَوَّابِيْنَ غَفُوْرًا‏(25)\nRRABBUKUM A-A’LAMO BEMAA FEE NUFOOSEKUM IN TAKOONOO SAALEHEENA FA-INNAHU KAANA LIL-AAWABEENA GHAFOORAR.\nYour Lord knoweth best what is in yourselves; if ye be righteous, then verily He is for the repentants Oft-Forgiving.\nوَاٰتِ ذَا الْقُرْبٰى حَقَّهٗ وَالْمِسْكِيْنَ وَابْنَ السَّبِيْلِ وَلَا تُبَذِّرْ تَبْذِيْرًا‏(26)\nWAATE ZAL QURBAA HAQQAHU WA MISKEENA WAB SABEELE WA LAA TUBAZZER TABZEERAN.\nAnd give to the near of kin his due and to the needy and the wayfarer, and squander not (thy earnings) wastefully.\nاِنَّ الْمُبَذِّرِيْنَ كَانُوْۤا اِخْوَانَ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ ؕ وَكَانَ الشَّيْطٰنُ لِرَبِّهٖ كَفُوْرًا‏(27)\nINNAL AL-MUBAZZEREENA KAANOO AEKHWAANA ASH-SHAYTEENE KAANAL SHAYTAANO LE-RABBEHI KAFOORAA.\nVerily the squanderers are the brethren of the satans; and Satan to his Lord is ever an ingrate.\nوَاِمَّا تُعْرِضَنَّ عَنْهُمُ ابْتِغَآءَ رَحْمَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ تَرْجُوْهَا فَقُلْ لَّهُمْ قَوْلًا مَّيْسُوْرًا‏(28)\nWA AMMAA TUA’REZANNA A’NHOMUL TEGHAAA-A RAHMATIN MIN RABBEKA TARJOOHAA FAQUL LAHUM QAWLAM MMAYSOORAN.\nIf thou (helplessly) turn away from them seeking mercy from thy Lord which thou hopest for, then speak unto them (at- least) a kindly word.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ يَدَكَ مَغْلُوْلَةً اِلٰى عُنُقِكَ وَلَا تَبْسُطْهَا كُلَّ الْبَسْطِ فَتَقْعُدَ مَلُوْمًا مَّحْسُوْرًا‏(29)\nWA LAA TAJ-A’L YADAKA MAGHLOOLATAN ELAA U’UNUQEKA WA LAA TABSUTHAA KULLA AL-BASTE FATAQU’UDA MALOOMAN MMAHSOORAN.\nAnd cause thou not to shackle thy hand unto thy neck, nor stretch it forth to the maximum (limits of) stretching forth, lest thou shouldst (thereafter) sit down blamed, destituted.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(30)\nINNAL RABBAKA YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER INNAHU KAANA BE-E’BAADEHI KHABEERAA BASEERAA.\nVerily thy Lord extendeth the sustenance for whomsoever He willeth and measureth it He (to a just measure); Verily He is, of His servants ever Fully- Aware, All-Seeing.\nوَلَا تَقْتُلُوْۤا اَوْلَادَكُمْ خَشْيَةَ اِمْلَاقٍؕ نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُهُمْ وَاِيَّاكُمْؕ اِنَّ قَتْلَهُمْ كَانَ خِطْاً كَبِيْرًا‏(31)\nWA LAA TAQTULOOA AWLAADAKUM KHASHYATA AEMLAAQIN NAHNO NARZUQUHUM WAAYYAAKUM INNAL QATLAHUM KAANA KHETAAN KABEERAA.\nAnd kill ye not your children for fear of want; We sustain them and yourselves (too); Verily killing them is a great sin.\nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوا الزِّنٰٓى اِنَّهٗ كَانَ فَاحِشَةً  ؕ وَسَآءَ سَبِيْلًا‏(32)\nWA LAA TAQRABOOA AZ-ZENAAA INNAHU KAANA FAAHESHATAN WA SAAA-A SABEELAA.\nAnd approach ye not adultery, Verily, it is a shameful act, and an evil way (opening to many other evils)\nوَلَا تَقْتُلُوا النَّفْسَ الَّتِىْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَمَنْ قُتِلَ مَظْلُوْمًا فَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا لِوَلِيِّهٖ سُلْطٰنًا فَلَا يُسْرِفْ فِّى الْقَتْلِ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مَنْصُوْرًا‏(33)\nWA LAA TAQTULOOA AN-NAFSA LATEE HARRAMA LAAHO ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA MAN QOTELAL MAZLOOMAN FAQAD JA-A’LNAA LEWALIYYEHI SULTAANAN FALAA YUSREF FFEAA QATL INNAHU KAANA MANSOORAN.\nAnd kill ye not any one whom God hath forbidden but for a just cause; and whoever is slain unjustly, then indeed have We given his heir the authority, but he shall not be extravagant in slaying; Verily he is aided (by God).\nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوْا مَالَ الْيَتِيْمِ اِلَّا بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ حَتّٰى يَبْلُغَ اَشُدَّهٗ وَاَوْفُوْا بِالْعَهْدِۚ اِنَّ الْعَهْدَ كَانَ مَسْئُوْلًا‏(34)\nWA LAA TAQRABOOA MAALA AL-YATEEME ILLAA BIL-LATEE HEYA AHSANO HATTAA HATTAA ASHUDDAHU WA AWFOO BIL-A’AHDE INNAL AL-A’AHDA KAANA MAS-OOLAA.\nAnd approach ye not the property of an orphan save in a way which is good until he attaineth his maturity and fulfil ye the promise; Verily (every) promise shall be questioned about.\nوَاَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ اِذَا كِلْتُمْ وَزِنُوْا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيْمِؕ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ وَّاَحْسَنُ تَاْوِيْلًا‏(35)\nWAAWFOOA AL-KAYLA EZAA KELTUM WAZENOOA BIL-QESTAASE AL-MUSTAQEEME ZAA LEKA KHAYRUL WWAAHSANU TAAWEELAN.\nAnd give ye full measure when ye measure out (anything) and weigh ye with a correct balance; This is good and the fairest in the end.\nوَلَا تَقْفُ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ ؕ اِنَّ السَّمْعَ وَالْبَصَرَ وَالْفُؤَادَ كُلُّ اُولٰۤئِكَ كَانَ عَنْهُ مَسْئُوْلًا‏(36)\nWA LAA TAQFU MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LMUM INNAL JA-A’LA WA BASARA WAL FUAADA KULLO AOOLAAEKA KAANA A’NHO MAS-OOLAA.\nAnd pursue thou not that which thou hast not the know ledge of; Verily, the hearing and the sight and the heart, all these shall be questioned about it.\nوَلَا تَمْشِ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَرَحًا ۚ اِنَّكَ لَنْ تَخْرِقَ الْاَرْضَ وَلَنْ تَبْلُغَ الْجِبَالَ طُوْلًا‏(37)\nWA LAA TAMSHE FIL ARZE MARAHAN INNAKA LAN TAKHREQA ARZA WA LAN TABLUGHA JEBAALA TOOLAN.\nAnd walk thou not on the earth exultingly; for thou (by thy insolence) canst not rend the earth nor reach (the heights of) the mountains in stretching (thyself).\nكُلُّ ذٰ لِكَ كَانَ سَيِّئُهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ مَكْرُوْهًا‏(38)\nKULLO ZAA LEKA KAANA SAYUH I’NDAL RABBEKA MAKROOHAN.\nAll this, the evil of it, with thy Lord is hateful.\nذٰ لِكَ مِمَّاۤ اَوْحٰۤى اِلَيْكَ رَبُّكَ مِنَ الْحِكْمَةِ ؕ وَلَا تَجْعَلْ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتُلْقٰى فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَلُوْمًا مَّدْحُوْرًا‏(39)\nZAA LEKA MIMMAA AAWHAA ELAYKA RABBOKA MENAL AL-HEKMATE WA LAA TAJ-A’L LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FATULQAA FEE JAHANNAMA MALOOMAN MMADHOORAN.\nThis of what thy Lord hath revealed unto thee of wisdom; and set not with God any other god lest thou be cast into the hell, blamed and cast away.\nاَفَاَصْفٰٮكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ بِالْبَنِيْنَ وَ اتَّخَذَ مِنَ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اِنَاثًا ؕ اِنَّكُمْ لَتَقُوْلُوْنَ قَوْلًا عَظِيْمًا‏(40)\nAAFAASFAAKUM RABBOKUM BIL-BANEENA WA TAKHAZA MENAL AL-MALAAEKATE AENAASAN INNAKUM LATAQOOLOONA QAWLAM A’ZEEMAA.\nWhat! has then your Lord preferred giving you sons, and taken (for Himself) daughters, from (among) the angels? Verily, ye utter an awful saying.\nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ لِيَذَّكَّرُوْا ؕ وَمَا يَزِيْدُهُمْ اِلَّا نُفُوْرًا‏(41)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAA FEE HAAZAA QUR-AANE LEEZZAKKAROOA WA MAA YAZEEDUHUM ILLAA NUFOORAN.\nAnd indeed have We displayed (the warnings) in this Qur’an that they might take heed; but it addeth not to them save aversion (against the truth).\nقُلْ لَّوْ كَانَ مَعَهٗۤ اٰلِهَةٌ كَمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِذًا لَّابْتَغَوْا اِلٰى ذِى الْعَرْشِ سَبِيْلًا‏(42)\nQUL LAW KAANA MA-A’HU AAALEHATUN KAMAA YAQOOLOONA EZAL LLAABTAGHAWA ELAA ZIL A’RSHIL SABEELAA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) If there were with Him (any) other gods (also) as they say, then certainly they would have been able to seek against the Lord of the ‘Arsh’ a way.\nسُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يَقُوْلُوْنَ عُلُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(43)\nWALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YAQOOLOONA O’LUWWAN KABEERAA.\nGlory be to Him and Exalted is He far above from what they say He is the High, and the Great.\nتُسَبِّحُ لَهُ السَّمٰوٰتُ السَّبْعُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهِنَّؕ وَاِنْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ اِلَّا يُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا تَفْقَهُوْنَ تَسْبِيْحَهُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ حَلِيْمًا غَفُوْرًا‏(44)\nTUSABBEHU LAHUL AS-SAMAAWAATU AS-SABU’U WAL WA MAN FEEHENNA WA MIN SHAY-IN ILLAA YOSABBEHO BEHAMDEH WA LAAKIL LAA TAFQAHOONA TASBEEHAHUM INNAHU KAANA HALEEMAA GHAFOORAR.\nCelebrate His glory the seven heavens and the earth, and (all) those in them; and there is not any thing but it glorifieth Him, but ye understand not their glorification; Verily, He is the Forbearing, the Oft-Forgiving.\nوَاِذَا قَرَاْتَ الْقُرْاٰنَ جَعَلْنَا بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ حِجَابًا مَّسْتُوْرًا ۙ‏(45)\nWA EZAA QARAA-TAL QUR-AANA JA-A’LNAA BAYNAKA WA BAYNAL LAZEENA LAA YOA-MINOONA BIL AAKHERATE HEJAABAM MASTOORAA.\nWhen thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) recitest the Qur’an We set between thee and those who believe not in the hereafter a hidden veil,\nوَّجَعَلْنَا عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ اَكِنَّةً اَنْ يَّفْقَهُوْهُ وَفِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ وَقْرًا ؕ وَاِذَا ذَكَرْتَ رَبَّكَ فِى الْقُرْاٰنِ وَحْدَهٗ وَلَّوْا عَلٰٓى اَدْبَارِهِمْ نُفُوْرًا‏(46)\nWA JA-A’LNAA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM AKINNATAN ANY YAFQAHOOHO WA FEE AAZAANEHIM WAQRAA, WA EZAA ZAKARTA RABBAKA FIL QUR-AANE WAHDAHU WALLAW A’LAA ADBAAREHIM NOFOORAA.\nAnd We have set on their hearts coverings lest they should understand it (the Qur’an) and in their ears a heaviness and when thou mentionest thy Lord alone, in (reciting) the Qur’an, turn they their backs in aversion.\nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ بِهٖۤ اِذْ يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ وَاِذْ هُمْ نَجْوٰٓى اِذْ يَقُوْلُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِنْ تَتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا رَجُلًا مَّسْحُوْرًا‏(47)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YASTAMEU’OONA BEHI IZ YASTAMEU’OONA ELAYKA WA IZ HUM NAJWAAA IZ YAQOOLO ZAALEMOON IN TATTABEU’OONA ILLAA RAJULAN MMASHOORAN.\nWe know best what they hearken, when they hearken unto thee, and when they are whispering secretly apart, when say the unjust (unto the believers): “Ye follow none but a man bewitched.\nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ ضَرَبُوْا لَكَ الْاَمْثَالَ فَضَلُّوْا فَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ سَبِيْلًا‏(48)\nAUNZUR KAYFA ZARABOOA LAKA AL-AAMSAALA FAZALLOOA FALAA YASTATEE-O’ONA SABEELAA.\nBehold thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) what similitudes they coin for thee! for they have gone (so far) astray (that) they can not find the way (to truth).\nوَقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا وَّرُفَاتًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ خَلْقًا جَدِيْدًا‏(49)\nWA QAALOO A-EZAA KUNNAA E’EZAAMAN WWARUFAATAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON KHALQAN JADEEDAN.\nAnd say they: “What! when we become (mere) bones and a decayed dust, shall we (even) then in fact be raised up into a new creation?\nقُلْ كُوْنُوْا حِجَارَةً اَوْ حَدِيْدًا‏(50)\nQUL KOONOO HEJAARATAN AW HADEEDAN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) (Even if) become ye stones or iron,\nاَوْ خَلْقًا مِّمَّا يَكْبُرُ فِىْ صُدُوْرِكُمْۚ فَسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَنْ يُّعِيْدُنَا ؕ قُلِ الَّذِىْ فَطَرَكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ۚ فَسَيُنْغِضُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ رُءُوْسَهُمْ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هُوَ ؕ قُلْ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ قَرِيْبًا‏(51)\nAW KHALQAN MIMMAA YAKBURU FEE SUDOOREKUM FASAYAQOOLOONA MAN YYUE’EEDUNAA QOLIL LAZEE FATARAKUM AWWALA MARRAH FASAYUNGHEZOONA ELAYKA RO-OOSAHUM WA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HOWA QUL A’SAA AN YAKOONA QAREEBAA.\nOr any other creature which seem yet harder to you (to receive life)”, But they will say “Who will cause us to return?” Say thou: “He Who created you first!” Then will they wag their heads unto thee and say: “When will that be?” Say thou “Maybe it is nigh.\nيَوْمَ يَدْعُوْكُمْ فَتَسْتَجِيْبُوْنَ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَتَظُنُّوْنَ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(52)\nYAWMA YADU’OOKUM FATASTAJEEBOONA BEHAMDEH HANAAJERA WA IN LLABESTUM ILLAA QALEELAA.\nOn the day when He will call you forth, and ye will respond with His praise and ye will think that ye tarried (in your graves) but a little (while).\nوَقُلْ لِّعِبَادِىْ يَقُوْلُوا الَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ يَنْزَغُ بَيْنَهُمْؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ كَانَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ عَدُوًّا مُّبِيْنًا‏(53)\nWA QUL LLEE’EBAADEAA YAQOOLOOA LATEE HEYA AAHSANU INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA YANZAGHU BAYNAHUM INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA KAANA INSAANIK A’DUWWAL MOBEENAA.\nAnd say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) unto My servants that they should utter (only) that which is best; Verily Satan soweth dissensions among them; Verily Satan unto man is an open enemy.\nرَبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِكُمْؕ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يَرْحَمْكُمْ اَوْ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يُعَذِّبْكُمْ ؕ وَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَكِيْلًا‏(54)\nRABBOKUM A-A’LAMO BEKUM IN YYASHAA YARHAMKUM AW IN YYASHAA QABLO WA MAA ARSALNAAKA A’LAYHIM WAKEELAA.\nYour Lord knoweth you best; If He willeth He will have mercy on you, and if He willeth He will chastise you; and We sent not thee to be a guardian over them (against the evils they do).\nوَرَبُّكَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ وَلَقَدْ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَ النَّبِيّٖنَ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ وَّاٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ زَبُوْرًا‏(55)\nWA RABBOKA A-A’LAMO BEMAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA LAQAD FAZZALNAA YAWM NABIYYEENA A’LAA ELAA WWAATAYNAA DAAWOODA ZABOORAN.\nAnd thy Lord knoweth best (all) those who are in the heavens and the earth; and indeed We have exalted some apostles to some (other apostles): and gave We unto David, ‘Zabur’ (the Psalter).\nقُلِ ادْعُوا الَّذِيْنَ زَعَمْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ فَلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ كَشْفَ الضُّرِّ عَنْكُمْ وَلَا تَحْوِيْلًا‏(56)\nQOLIL ADU’OOA LAZEENA ZA-A’MTUM MIN DOONEHI FALAA YAMLEKOONA KASHFA AZ-ZURRE A’NKUM WA LAA TAHWEELAN.\nSay thou: “Call ye those whom ye fancy (to be gods) other than Him: they shall neither have the power of removing the distress from you nor (even) to alter it.\nاُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ يَبْتَغُوْنَ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمُ الْوَسِيْلَةَ اَيُّهُمْ اَقْرَبُ وَيَرْجُوْنَ رَحْمَتَهٗ وَيَخَافُوْنَ عَذَابَهٗؕ اِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ كَانَ مَحْذُوْرًا‏(57)\nAOOLAAEKA LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA YABTAGHOONA ELAA RABBEHEMU AL-WASEELATA AAYHUM AQRABO WA YARJOON RAHMATAH WA YAKHAAFOONA A’AZAABAH INNAL A’ZAABAL RABBEKA KAANA MAHZOORAN.\nThose whom they call, to seek the access unto their Lord (to know) which of them is the nearest (to Him) and hope they for His mercy, and fear they His chastisement; Verily, the chastisement of thy Lord is to be dreaded of.\nوَاِنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اِلَّا نَحْنُ مُهْلِكُوْهَا قَبْلَ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ اَوْ مُعَذِّبُوْهَا عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا ؕ كَانَ ذٰ لِكَ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مَسْطُوْرًا‏(58)\nWA MIN QARYATINW ILLAA NAHNO MUHLEKOOHAA QABLA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE AW MUA’AZZEBOOHAA A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAA KAANA ZAA LEKA FIL KETAABE MASTOORAN.\nAnd there is not a town but We shall destroy it before the Day of Judgment or chastise it with a severe chastisement; that is written in the Book (of Our Will).\nوَمَا مَنَعَنَاۤ اَنْ نُّرْسِلَ بِالْاٰيٰتِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ كَذَّبَ بِهَا الْاَوَّلُوْنَؕ وَاٰتَيْنَا ثَمُوْدَ النَّاقَةَ مُبْصِرَةً فَظَلَمُوْا بِهَاؕ وَمَا نُرْسِلُ بِالْاٰيٰتِ اِلَّا تَخْوِيْفًا‏(59)\nWA MAA MANAA’ANAA AN NNURSELA BE-AAYAATE ILLAA AN KAZZABA BEHAA AL-AAWLOONA WA AATAYNAA ELAA AN-NAAQATA MUBSERATAN FA ZALAMOO BEHAA WA MAA NURSELU BE-AAYAATE ILLAA TAKHWEEFAN.\nAnd nothing hindereth Us that We should send signs save that belied them the ancients; and gave We unto Thamud the She-Camel, an open sign but unto her they did injustice; and We send not signs but to warn (the people).\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لَكَ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ اَحَاطَ بِالنَّاسِ ؕ وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الرُّءْيَا الَّتِىْۤ اَرَيْنٰكَ اِلَّا فِتْنَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَ الشَّجَرَةَ الْمَلْعُوْنَةَ فِى الْقُرْاٰنِ ؕ وَنُخَوِّفُهُمْۙ فَمَا يَزِيْدُهُمْ اِلَّا طُغْيَانًا كَبِيْرًا‏(60)\nWA IZ QULNAL LAKA INNAL RABBAKA AHAATAL BIN-NAASE WA MAA JA-A’LNAA RO-YAA LATEE AARAYNAAKA ILLAA FETNATAN LIN-NAASE WA SHAJARATA AL-MALU’OONATA FIL QUR-AANE WANUKHAWFUHUM FAMAA YAZEEDUHUM ILLAA TUGHYAANAN KABEERAA.\nAnd (recollect thou O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) when said We unto thee: “Verily, thy Lord encompasseth the people;” and We caused not the vision which We shewed thee save as a trial for the people, and (similarly) the Accursed Tree in the Qur’an; and We cause them to fear, but it addeth not to them but their grievous transgression.\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَ قَالَ ءَاَسْجُدُ لِمَنْ خَلَقْتَ طِيْنًا ۚ‏(61)\nWA IZ QULNAL LIL-MALAAEKATE JODOO LE-AADAMA FASAJADOOA ILLAA AEBLEESA QAALA AASJUDU LEMAN-Y KHALAQTA TEENAN.\nAnd (remember O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when said We unto the angels: “Prostrate ye (in obeisance) to Adam!” Prostrated all (of them) but ‘Iblis’ (who did it not) said he: “(What!) Am I to prostrate unto him whom Thou hast created of clay?\nقَالَ اَرَءَيْتَكَ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كَرَّمْتَ عَلَىَّ لَئِنْ اَخَّرْتَنِ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَاَحْتَنِكَنَّ ذُرِّيَّتَهٗۤ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(62)\nQAALA AARAAYTAKA HAAZAA LAZEE KARRAMTA A’LAYYA LAIL AAKKHARTANE ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAAHTANEKANNA ZURREETAH ILLAA QALEELAA.\nHe (Iblis) said: “Seest Thou, (This) is (the creature) whom Thou hath honoured above me? If thou respiteth me until the Day of Judgment, I will sever his posterity (under my sway) from its origin save a few.\nقَالَ اذْهَبْ فَمَنْ تَبِعَكَ مِنْهُمْ فَاِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ جَزَآؤُكُمْ جَزَآءً مَّوْفُوْرًا‏(63)\nQAALA AZHAB FAMAN TABEA’AKA MINHUM FA-INNAL JAHANNAMA JAZAAUKUM JA-ZAAA-AWN MMAWFOORAN.\nSaid He: “Begone! But whosoever of them followeth thee, then verily Hell is your recompense, a recompense in full!\nوَاسْتَفْزِزْ مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ مِنْهُمْ بِصَوْتِكَ وَاَجْلِبْ عَلَيْهِمْ بِخَيْلِكَ وَرَجِلِكَ وَشَارِكْهُمْ فِى الْاَمْوَالِ وَالْاَوْلَادِ وَعِدْهُمْ ؕ وَمَا يَعِدُهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اِلَّا غُرُوْرًا‏(64)\nWAASTAFZEZ MANIS ASTATAA’TA MINHUM BESAWTEKA WAAJLEB A’LAYHIM BEKHAYLEKA WARAJELEKA WASHAAREKHUM FIL AMWAALE WAL WAL AAWLAADE WAE’EDHUM WA MAA YAE’EDUHUMU SHAYTAANO ILLAA GHOROORAA.\nAnd tear thou away whomsoever of them thou canst with thy voice, and collect (against) them thy cavalry and infantry, and partake with them in (their) riches and (their) children, and make promises unto them;” and promiseth not unto them the Satan but a deceit.\nاِنَّ عِبَادِىْ لَيْسَ لَكَ عَلَيْهِمْ سُلْطٰنٌ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ وَكِيْلًا‏(65)\nINNAL E’BAADEE LAYSA LAKA A’LAYHIM SULTAANUN KAFAA BERABBEKA WAKEELAA.\nVerily (as for) My (own) servants, thou shalt not have over them any authority, and sufficeth thy Lord (as their) Guardian.\nرَبُّكُمُ الَّذِىْ يُزْجِىْ لَكُمُ الْفُلْكَ فِى الْبَحْرِ لِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِكُمْ رَحِيْمًا‏(66)\nRABBUKUMU LAZEE YUZJEAA LAKOMUL AL-FULKA FIL BAHRE LE-TABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEH INNAHU KAANA BEKUM RAHEEMAA.\nYour Lord is He who saileth the ships for you in the sea that ye may seek of His grace; Verily He is ever unto you the Most Merciful.\nوَاِذَا مَسَّكُمُ الضُّرُّ فِى الْبَحْرِ ضَلَّ مَنْ تَدْعُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُ ۚ فَلَمَّا نَجّٰٮكُمْ اِلَى الْبَرِّ اَعْرَضْتُمْ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ كَفُوْرًا‏(67)\nWA EZAA MASSAKUMU AZ-ZURRU FIL BAHRE ZALLA MAN TADU’OONA ILLAA IYYAAHO FALAMMAA NAJJAAKUM ELAL BARRE AAA’RAZTUM KAANAL INSAANO KAFOORAA.\nWhen toucheth you any distress in the sea, away go those whom ye invoke, save He (alone) yet when He bringeth you safe unto the land ye turn away (from Him); and man hath ever been ungrateful.\nاَفَاَمِنْتُمْ اَنْ يَّخْسِفَ بِكُمْ جَانِبَ الْبَرِّ اَوْ يُرْسِلَ عَلَيْكُمْ حَاصِبًا ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُوْالَكُمْ وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(68)\nAAFAAMENTUM AN YAKHSEFA BEKUM JAANEBA BARRE AW YURSELA A’LAYKUM HAASEBAN SUMMA LAA TAJEDOOALAKUM WAKEELAA.\nWhat! feel ye then secure that He will (not) cause the slope of the earth for you (to be swallowed up) I or that He will (not) send against you a violent wind showering stones (on you), then ye shall find not for you any protector.\nاَمْ اَمِنْتُمْ اَنْ يُّعِيْدَكُمْ فِيْهِ تَارَةً اُخْرٰى فَيُرْسِلَ عَلَيْكُمْ قَاصِفًا مِّنَ الرِّيْحِ فَيُغْرِقَكُمْ بِمَا كَفَرْتُمْۙ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُوْا لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا بِهٖ تَبِيْعًا‏(69)\nAM AMINTUM AN YYUE’EEDAKUM FEEHE TAARATAN LAHU FAYURSELA A’LAYKUM QAASEFAN MENAL AR-REEHE FAYUGHREQAKUM BEMAA KAFARTUM SUMMA LAA WA LAM LAKUM A’LAYNAA BEHI TABEEA’AN.\nOr feel ye secure that He will (not) take you back into it (the sea) another time, and then send on you a fierce gale and drown you for what ye disbelieved, then ye shall find not against Us any pleader\nوَلَقَدْ كَرَّمْنَا بَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ وَحَمَلْنٰهُمْ فِى الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ وَرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَفَضَّلْنٰهُمْ عَلٰى كَثِيْرٍ مِّمَّنْ خَلَقْنَا تَفْضِيْلًا‏(70)\nWA LAQAD KARRAMNAA BANEE AADAMAL WAHAMALNAAHUM FIL BARRE WAL BAHRE WA RAZAQNAAHUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE WAFAZZALNAAHUM A’LAA KASEERIM MIMMAYN KHALAQNAL TAFZEELAN.\nAnd indeed We have honoured the children of Adam, and We carry them in the land and on the sea and We provided them with sustenance of good things, and We have exalted them over most of those whom We have created, by (high) decree of exaltation.\nيَوْمَ نَدْعُوْا كُلَّ اُنَاسٍۢ بِاِمَامِهِمْۚ فَمَنْ اُوْتِىَ كِتٰبَهٗ بِيَمِيْنِهٖ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ يَقْرَءُوْنَ كِتٰبَهُمْ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ فَتِيْلًا‏(71)\nYAWMA NADU’OOA KULLA ONAASIM BEAEMAAMEHEM FAMAN OOTEYA KETAABAHU BE-YAMEENEHI FAAWLAAEKA YAQRAOONA KETAABAHUM WA LAA LAA YUZLAMOON FATEELAN.\nRemember the Day (of Judgment) when We will summon every people with their Imam (Leader); then whosoever is given his book in his right hand, these shall read their books (with pleasure), and they shall not be dealt with (even) a shred unjustly.\nوَمَنْ كَانَ فِىْ هٰذِهٖۤ اَعْمٰى فَهُوَ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اَعْمٰى وَاَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(72)\nWA MAN KAANA FEE HAAZEHI AAA’MAA FAHOWA FIL AAKHERATE AAA’MAA WA AZALLO SABEELAA.\nAnd whosoever is blind in this (life), he shall in the hereafter (also) be blind and gone further astray from the (right) way.\nوَاِنْ كَادُوْا لَيَفْتِنُوْنَكَ عَنِ الَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ لِتَفْتَرِىَ عَلَيْنَا غَيْرَهٗ ۖ  وَاِذًا لَّاتَّخَذُوْكَ خَلِيْلًا‏(73)\nWA KAADOO LAYAFTENOONAKA A’NIL LAZEE AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA LETAFTAREAAA A’LAYNAA GHAYRAH WA EZAL LLAATTAKHAZOOKA KHALEELAN.\nAnd verily they had well-nigh purposed to turn thee away from that which We have revealed unto thee, that thou shouldst forge against Us other than that, and then they would surely have taken thee as a friend.\nوَلَوْلَاۤ اَنْ ثَبَّتْنٰكَ لَقَدْ كِدْتَّ تَرْكَنُ اِلَيْهِمْ شَيْئًا قَلِيْلًا  ۙ‏(74)\nWA LAWLAA AN SABBATNAAKA LAQAD KEDTTA TARKANU ELAYHIM SHAY-ANW QALEELAA.\nAnd if it was not that We had firmly established thee, thou wouldst surely had been nigh to incline unto them a little,\nاِذًا لَّاَذَقْنٰكَ ضِعْفَ الْحَيٰوةِ وَضِعْفَ الْمَمَاتِ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُ لَكَ عَلَيْنَا نَصِيْرًا‏(75)\nEZAL LLAAZAQNAAKA ZEA’FA HAYAATID WAZEA’FA AL-MAMAATE SUMMA LAA TAJEDU LAKA A’LAYNAA NASEERAA.\nIn that case We would surely have caused thee taste a double (torment) in this life and a double (torment) after death, (and) then thou wouldst not have found for thee against Us any helper.\nوَاِنْ كَادُوْا لَيَسْتَفِزُّوْنَكَ مِنَ الْاَرْضِ لِيُخْرِجُوْكَ مِنْهَا وَاِذًا لَّا يَلْبَثُوْنَ خِلٰفَكَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(76)\nWA KAADOO LAYASTAFEZZOONAKA MENAL ARZE LEEKHREJOOKA MINHAA WA EZAL LAA YALBASOONA KHELAAFAKA ILLAA QALEELAA.\nAnd verily well-nigh they purposed to tare these away from the land, that they might drive thee out from it, but then, they would not have tarried (therein) after thee, but a little.\nسُنَّةَ مَنْ قَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ مِنْ رُّسُلِنَا وَلَا تَجِدُ لِسُنَّتِنَا تَحْوِيْلًا‏(77)\nSUNNATAL MAN QAD ARSALNAA QABLAKA MIN RRUSULENAA WA LAA TAJEDU LESUNNATENAA TAHWEELAN.\nThis was Our way with those of Our apostles whom We did send before thee, and thou shalt find not in Our way any change.\nاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ لِدُلُوْكِ الشَّمْسِ اِلٰى غَسَقِ الَّيْلِ وَقُرْاٰنَ الْفَجْرِؕ اِنَّ قُرْاٰنَ الْفَجْرِ كَانَ مَشْهُوْدًا‏(78)\nAAQEME SALAATA LEDULOOKE ASH-SHAMSE ELAA GHASAQE LAYLE WAQURAAANA FAJR INNAL QURAAANA FAJR KAANA MASHHOODAN.\nEstablish prayer (regularly) from the declension of the sun till the darkness of the night, and the recital at the morn; verily the recital at the morn is witnessed.\nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَتَهَجَّدْ بِهٖ نَافِلَةً لَّكَ ۖ  عَسٰۤى اَنْ يَّبْعَثَكَ رَبُّكَ مَقَامًا مَّحْمُوْدًا‏(79)\nWA MENAN LAYLE FATAHAJJAD BEHI NAAFELATAN LAKA A’SAA AN YYABA’ASAKA RABBOKA MAQAAMAN MMAHMOODAN.\nAnd (in a part) of the night, forsake sleep for prayer, in addition to (what is incumbent on) thee; Maybe that exalteth thee thy Lord unto a position praised.\nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَدْخِلْنِىْ مُدْخَلَ صِدْقٍ وَّ اَخْرِجْنِىْ مُخْرَجَ صِدْقٍ وَّاجْعَلْ لِّىْ مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ سُلْطٰنًا نَّصِيْرًا‏(80)\nWA QUL RABBIL AADKHELNEAA MUDKHALA SEDQIN WA AAKHREJNEAA MUKHRAJA SEDQIN WWAAJA’AL LEE MIN LLADUNKA SULTAANAN NNASEERAN.\nAnd say thou (praying): “O’ My Lord! cause me to enter a goodly entrance and cause me to go out (of) a goodly exit, and grant me from unto Thee an authority to assist (me)\nوَقُلْ جَآءَ الْحَقُّ وَزَهَقَ الْبَاطِلُؕ اِنَّ الْبَاطِلَ كَانَ زَهُوْقًا‏(81)\nWA QUL JAAA-A HAQQO WAZAHAQA AL-BAATELU INNAL AL-BAATELA KAANA ZAHOOQAN.\nAnd say thou “The truth hath come and the falsehood hath vanished; Verily falsehood is (a thing by nature) vanishing.\nوَنُنَزِّلُ مِنَ الْقُرْاٰنِ مَا هُوَ شِفَآءٌ وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ وَلَا يَزِيْدُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ اِلَّا خَسَارًا‏(82)\nWANUNAZZELU MENAL QUR-AANE MAA HOWA SHEFAAUN WA RAHMATUL LIL-MOAMENEEN WA LAA YAZEEDU ZAALEMEEN ILLAA KHASAARAN.\nAnd We sent down of the Qur’an which is a healing and a mercy unto the believers, but it addeth not to the unjust but perdition.\nوَاِذَاۤ اَنْعَمْنَا عَلَى الْاِنْسَانِ اَعْرَضَ وَنَاٰ بِجَانِبِهٖۚ وَاِذَا مَسَّهُ الشَّرُّ كَانَ يَئُوْسًا‏(83)\nWA EZAA AN-A’MNAA A’LAL INSAANE A-A’RAZA WA NA-AA BEJAANEBEH WA EZAA MASSAHUSH SHARRO KAANA YAOOSAN.\nAnd when bestow We our bounties on man, he turneth aside and goeth away (on the reverse) and when toucheth him any evil, he is despondent.\nقُلْ كُلٌّ يَّعْمَلُ عَلٰى شَاكِلَتِهٖؕ فَرَبُّكُمْ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ هُوَ اَهْدٰى سَبِيْلًا‏(84)\nQUL KULLUL YYAA’MALU A’LAA SHAAKELATEH FA RABBOKUM A-A’LAMO BEMAN HOWA AHDAA SABEELAA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad! unto the people): “Every one acteth after his own mould; thus your Lord best knoweth (as to) who (among you) is the best guide of the right path.\nوَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الرُّوْحِ ؕ قُلِ الرُّوْحُ مِنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّىْ وَمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا‏(85)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL AR-ROOHE QOLIL ROOHO MIN AMRE RABBEE WA MAA MAA OOTEETUM MENAL I’LME ILLAA QALEELAA.\nAnd they ask thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) about the spirit, Say thou “The spirit is, from the command of my Lord, and ye are not given of the knowledge but a little.\nوَلَئِنْ شِئْنَا لَنَذْهَبَنَّ بِالَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ ثُمَّ لَا تَجِدُ لَكَ بِهٖ عَلَيْنَا وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(86)\nWA LAIN SHE’NAA LANAZHABANNA BIL-LAZEE AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA SUMMA LAA TAJEDU LAKA BEHI A’LAYNAA WAKEELAA.\nAnd if We please, We would certainly take away that which We revealed unto thee, then thou wouldst find not for thee against Us any pleader,\nاِلَّا رَحْمَةً مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ ؕ اِنَّ فَضْلَهٗ كَانَ عَلَيْكَ كَبِيْرًا‏(87)\nILLAA RAHMATAM MIN RABBEKA INNAL FAZLAH KAANA A’LAYKA KABEERAA.\nSave the mercy from thy Lord: Verily, His grace on thee is (ever) great.\nقُلْ لَّئِنِ اجْتَمَعَتِ الْاِنْسُ وَالْجِنُّ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتُوْا بِمِثْلِ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ لَا يَاْتُوْنَ بِمِثْلِهٖ وَلَوْ كَانَ بَعْضُهُمْ لِبَعْضٍ ظَهِيْرًا‏(88)\nQUL LLAENE AJTAMAA’ATE AL-AENSU WAL JENNU A’LAA AN YYAATOOA BE-MISLE HAAZAA QUR-AANE LAA YAATOONAL BEMESLEH WA LAW KAANA KHALAA LE-BA’ZIN ZAHEERAL.\nSay thou “(Even) if men and the jinn get united (with the object) that they bring the like of this Qur’an, they would bring not the like of it, even though some of them to the others be helpers.\nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنَا لِلنَّاسِ فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ كُلِّ مَثَلٍ فَاَبٰٓى اَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(89)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAA LIN-NAASE FEE HAAZAA QUR-AANE MIN KULLE MASALIN FAABAAA AAKSARU NAASE ILLAA KUFOORAN.\nAnd indeed have We displayed unto the people, in this Qur’an, every (kind of) example but incline not most of the people save denying.\nوَقَالُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتّٰى تَفْجُرَ لَنَا مِنَ الْاَرْضِ يَنْۢبُوْعًا ۙ‏(90)\nWA QAALOO LAN NOAMENA LAKA HATTAA TAFJURA LANAA MENAL ARZE YANBOOA’AN.\nAnd said they: “Never will we believe in thee until thou causeth a spring for us from the earth to gush forth,\nاَوْ تَكُوْنَ لَكَ جَنَّةٌ مِّنْ نَّخِيْلٍ وَّعِنَبٍ فَتُفَجِّرَ الْاَنْهٰرَ خِلٰلَهَا تَفْجِيْرًا ۙ‏(91)\nAW TAKOONA LAKA JANNATUM MIN NAKHEELINW WWAE’ENABIN FATUFAJJERA AL-AANHAARA JA-A’LA TAFJEERAN.\nOr (cause it to) be for thee a garden of date-palms and grapes, and (cause) rivers in their midst, gushing forth,\nاَوْ تُسْقِطَ السَّمَآءَ كَمَا زَعَمْتَ عَلَيْنَا كِسَفًا اَوْ تَاْتِىَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ قَبِيْلًا ۙ‏(92)\nAW TUSQETA SAMAAA-AD KAMAA ZAA’AMTA A’LAYNAA KESAFAN AW TAATEAAA BIL-LAAHE WAL MALAAEKATE QABEELAN.\nOr cause the heavens to fall as thou didst assert upon us, in pieces, or bring thou God and the angels (to vouch for thee) face to face (with us),\nاَوْ يَكُوْنَ لَكَ بَيْتٌ مِّنْ زُخْرُفٍ اَوْ تَرْقٰى فِى السَّمَآءِ ؕ وَلَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لِرُقِيِّكَ حَتّٰى تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيْنَا كِتٰبًا نَّقْرَؤُهٗ ؕ قُلْ سُبْحَانَ رَبِّىْ هَلْ كُنْتُ اِلَّا بَشَرًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(93)\nAW YAKOONA LAKA BAYTUN MIN ZUKHRUFIN AW TARQAA FIL SAMAAA-E WA LAN NOAMENA LERUQEEKA HATTAA TUNAZZELA A’LAYNAA KETAABAA NNAQRAUH QUL SUBHAANA RABBEE HAL KUNTO ILLAA BASHARAN RASOOLANY.\nOr there be for thee a house of gold, or ascend thou into the heaven; and never will we believe in thy ascending until thou causeth to be sent down unto us a book that we may read it. “Say: thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!)” “Glory be to my Lord; am I aught save a man (sent by God as) Apostle.\nوَمَا مَنَعَ النَّاسَ اَنْ يُّؤْمِنُوْۤا اِذْ جَآءَهُمُ الْهُدٰٓى اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اَبَعَثَ اللّٰهُ بَشَرًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(94)\nWA MAA MANAA’A NAASA AN YOAMENOO IZ JAAA-AHOMUL HODAA ILLAA AN QAALOO AABAA’ASA LAAHO BASHARAN RASOOLANY.\nAnd nothing prevented the people from believing, when came unto them the guidance (from their Lord), save that they said: “What! hath God sent a man (like unto us to be) (His) Apostle.\nقُلْ لَّوْ كَانَ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَلٰۤئِكَةٌ يَّمْشُوْنَ مُطْمَئِنِّيْنَ لَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ مَلَكًا رَّسُوْلًا‏(95)\nQUL LAW KAANA FIL ARZE MALAAEKATUN YYAMSHOONA MUTMAENNEENA LANAZZALNAA A’LAYHIM MENAL SAMAAA-E MALAKAN RASOOLANY.\nSay thou: “If there were in the earth angels walking, settled in security, surely We would have sent down unto them, from the heaven, an angel as an apostle.\nقُلْ كَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًۢا بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًۢا بَصِيْرًا‏(96)\nQUL KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM INNAHU KAANA BE-E’BAADEHI KHABEERAA BASEERAA.\nSay thou: “Sufficeth God as a witness between me and you; Verily He of His servants is All- Aware and All-Seeing.\nوَمَنْ يَّهْدِ اللّٰهُ فَهُوَ الْمُهْتَدِ ۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلْ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لَهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ ؕ وَنَحْشُرُهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْ عُمْيًا وَّبُكْمًا وَّصُمًّا ؕ مَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ ؕ كُلَّمَا خَبَتْ زِدْنٰهُمْ سَعِيْرًا‏(97)\nWA MAN YYAHDE LAAHO FAHOWA AL-MUHTADE WA MAN YYUZLEL FALAN TAJEDA LAHUM AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONEHI WANAHSHURUHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE A’LAA SEEMAAHUM U’UMYAN WWABUKMAN WWASUMMAN MAAWAAHUM JAHANNAMUL KULLAMAA KHABAT ZEDNAAHUM SA-E’ERAA.\nAnd whomsoever God guideth, then he is guided aright; and whomsoever He leaveth to stray, thou shalt never find for him any guardians other than Him; and We will gather them together on the Day of Resurrection on their faces, blind dumb and deaf; their abode shall be Hell; so oft as it abateth, We shall increase for them the blaze.\nذٰلِكَ جَزَآؤُهُمْ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا وَّرُفَاتًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ خَلْقًا جَدِيْدًا‏(98)\nZAALEKA JAZAAUHUM BE-ANNAHUM KAFAROO BE-AAYAATENAA WA QAALOO A-EZAA KUNNAA E’EZAAMAN WWARUFAATAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON KHALQAN JADEEDAN.\nThis is their recompense for they disbelieved in Our signs and said they: “What! when we become (mere) bones and decayed dust, (even) then shall we (in fact) be raised into a new creation?\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ قَادِرٌ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّخْلُقَ مِثْلَهُمْ وَجَعَلَ لَهُمْ اَجَلًا لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ ؕ فَاَبَى الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(99)\nAWALAM YARAW ANNAL LAAHA LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA QAADERUN A’LAA AN ANY-YAKHLOQA MESLAHUM WA LAHUM AAJALAN LAA RAYBA FEEHE FAABAA ZAALEMOON ILLAA KUFOORAN.\nWhat! See they not that God Who created the heavens and the earth, is (certainly) able to create the like of them, and He hath decreed for them a term in which there is no doubt; but incline not the unjust save (to) denying.\nقُلْ لَّوْ اَنْتُمْ تَمْلِكُوْنَ خَزَآئِنَ رَحْمَةِ رَبِّىْۤ اِذًا لَّاَمْسَكْتُمْ خَشْيَةَ الْاِنْفَاقِ ؕ وَكَانَ الْاِنْسَانُ قَتُوْرًا‏(100)\nQUL LAW ANTUM TAMLEKOONA KHAZAAENA RAHMATE RABBEE EZAL LLAAMSAKTUM KHASHYATA AL-AENFAAQE KAANAL INSAANO QATOORAN.\nSay thou: If ye own the treasures of the mercy of my Lord, (even) then will ye certainly withhold them for fear of spending; and man is ever niggardly.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسٰى تِسْعَ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍ فَسْئَلْ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ اِذْ جَآءَهُمْ فَقَالَ لَهٗ فِرْعَوْنُ اِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّكَ يٰمُوْسٰى مَسْحُوْرًا‏(101)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAA TESA’A AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT FASAL BANEE AESRAAEELA IZ JAAA-AHUM FAQAALA LAHU FIRA’WNO INNEE LAAZUNNUKA YAA MOOSAA MASHOORAN.\nAnd indeed We gave Moses nine clear signs (miracles); so ask the children of Israel when he came unto them, Pharaoh said unto him; “Verily I deem thee O’ Moses one bewitched\nقَالَ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اِلَّا رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ بَصَآئِرَ ۚ وَاِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّكَ يٰفِرْعَوْنُ مَثْبُوْرًا‏(102)\nQAALA LAQAD A’ALEMTA MAA ANZALAL HAAOOLAAA-E ILLAA RABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE BASAAA-ERA WA INNEE LAAZUNNUKA YAA FIRA’WNO MASBOORAN.\nSaid he Indeed, thou knowest that none hath sent these down save the Lord of the heavens and the earth (as) eye opening proofs; and I think thou O’ Pharaoh is doomed to perdition.\nفَاَرَادَ اَنْ يَّسْتَفِزَّهُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ فَاَغْرَقْنٰهُ وَ مَنْ مَّعَهٗ جَمِيْعًا ۙ‏(103)\nFA ARAADA AN YYASTAFEZZAHUM MENAL ARZE FAAGHRAQNAAHU WA MAN MMAA’AH JAMEE-A’A.\nAnd resolved he to tare them away out of the land, so We drowned him and those with him, all together,\nوَّقُلْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ لِبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ اسْكُنُوا الْاَرْضَ فَاِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ الْاٰخِرَةِ جِئْنَا بِكُمْ لَفِيْفًا ؕ‏(104)\nWWAQULNAA MIN BA’DEHI LE-BANEE AESRAAEELA ASKUNOOA ARZA FA-EZAA JAAA-A WAA’DU AAKHERATE JENAA BEKUM LAFEEFAN.\nAnd said We after that, unto the children of Israel: “Abide ye in peace in the land, but when cometh the later promise, We shall bring you all rolled up (collected together)\nوَبِالْحَقِّ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ وَبِالْحَقِّ نَزَلَ ؕ وَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا ۘ‏(105)\nWA BIL-HAQQE ANZALNAAHO WA BIL-HAQQE NAZALA WA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA MUBASSHERAN WA NAZEERANW.\nAnd with truth have We sent it down and with truth it hath come down; and We sent not thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) but as a Giver of glad tidings and as a Warner.\nوَقُرْاٰنًا فَرَقْنٰهُ لِتَقْرَاَهٗ عَلَى النَّاسِ عَلٰى مُكْثٍ وَّنَزَّلْنٰهُ تَنْزِيْلًا‏(106)\nWA QURAANAN FARAQNAAHU LETAQRAAH A’LAL NAASE A’LAA MUKSIN WWANAZZALNAAHU TANZEELAA.\nAnd it is Qur’an which We have apportioned it so that thou mayest recite it unto the people with deliberation (by degrees), and We have sent it down, gradually in portions.\nقُلْ اٰمِنُوْا بِهٖۤ اَوْ لَا تُؤْمِنُوْٓا ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖۤ اِذَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ يَخِرُّوْنَ لِلْاَذْقَانِ سُجَّدًا ۙ‏(107)\nQUL AAMENOO BEHI AW LAA TUMENOOA INNAL LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA MIN QABLEHI EZAA YUTLAA A’LAYHIM YAKHERROONA LIL-AAZQAANE SUJJADANW.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Believe ye in it or believe ye not; Verily those who are (already) given the knowledge from before it, when it is recited unto them they fall down on their faces prostrating in obeisance,\nوَّيَقُوْلُوْنَ سُبْحٰنَ رَبِّنَاۤ اِنْ كَانَ وَعْدُ رَبِّنَا لَمَفْعُوْلًا‏(108)\nWWAYAQOOLOONA LAAHE RABBENAA IN KAANA WAA’DU RABBENAA LAMAFU’OOLAN.\nAnd say they: “Glorious is our Lord! verily the promise of our Lord was (a certainty) to be fulfilled.\nوَيَخِرُّوْنَ لِلْاَذْقَانِ يَبْكُوْنَ وَيَزِيْدُهُمْ خُشُوْعًا ۩‏(109)\nWAYAKHERROONA LIL-AAZQAANE YABKOONA WAYAZEEDUHUM KHUSHOOA’AN.\nAnd they fall down on their faces weeping and it (the listening to the Qur’an) increaseth their humility.\nقُلِ ادْعُوا اللّٰهَ اَوِ ادْعُوا الرَّحْمٰنَ ؕ اَ يًّا مَّا تَدْعُوْا فَلَهُ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰى ۚ وَلَا تَجْهَرْ بِصَلَاتِكَ وَلَا تُخَافِتْ بِهَا وَابْتَغِ بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ سَبِيْلًا‏(110)\nQOLIL ADU’OOA LAAHA AWE’ ADU’OOA BIL-GHAYBE A’ZAABAN YYAN MAA TADU’OOA FA LAHUL ASMAA-UL AL-HUSNAA WA LAA TAJHAR BESALAATEKA WA LAA TUKHAAFET BEHAA WABTAGHE BAYNA ZAA LEKA SABEELAA.\nSay: “Call upon ‘Allah’ (God) or call upon ‘Rahman’ (the Beneficent); whichever ye call upon, for Him (alone) are all the best names; and say thou not thy prayer too aloud, nor say it in too low a voice, but seek between these (extremes) a middle course.\nوَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَمْ يَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا وَّلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ شَرِيْكٌ فِى الْمُلْكِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ وَلِىٌّ مِّنَ الذُّلِّ وَكَبِّرْهُ تَكْبِيْرًا‏(111)\nWA HAMDO LILLAAHE LAZEE LAM YATTAKHEZ LAAHO LAM YAKUL LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL AL-MULKE WA LAM YAKUL LAHU WALIYYUN MENAL AZ-ZULLE WAKABBERHU TAKBEERAN.\nAnd say thou: “(All) Praise is God’s, Who hath not taken unto Him a son and Who hath not a partner in the kingdom, and there is not for Him any helper against any humility, and proclaim thou His Greatness magnifying (His Glory).",
  "merits": "Surah Bani Israaeel\nThere are 111 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that a great reward will be accorded to those who recite this Surah and when they reach the verse about parents, they feel a sense of love and gentleness towards their parents.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah Bani Israeel every Thursday night, will not die before meeting Imam Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) and will be counted among his companions. Also, if a child is not able to speak or is delaying in his learning how to speak, he should be given the water of this Surah that has been written with saffron.\nIn the commentary of Safi it is written that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) told Imam Ali (a.s.) that the last two verses of this Surah are a protection and safety from theft. This Surah is also called Surah al-Isra’."
